<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Basis values steady-lower.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Basis values steady-lower.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soymeal markets were quiet with some basis values slipping in reaction to competition from other feed ingredients, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;I think domestic demand is a lot lower. We are seeing a lot of competing products going to rations,&quot; said a Midwest dealer.</p>
<p>The competing ingredients include distillers grain, corn gluten feed, cottonseed meal and peanut meal, dealers said.</p>
<p>The weekly National Oilseed Processors Association crush of 24.568 million bushels was considered bearish by some dealers, who said domestic soymeal demand was edging down.  </p>
